commit(k,t,rows,marks,['text|upper left|4','diagram|upper left|Gd to G; ζd to ζ; Gd to G; Gd prime to G prime','diagram|left of group diagram|Z to ζ=Z/2Z','display|below group diagram|H2(X,ζ)','drawing|between upper blocks|curved separator and two diagonal arrows','drawing|under group block|blue wavy stroke','diagram|upper right|cohomology comparison with W and half W','display|upper-right corner|ζu','deletion|under upper left cohomology node|Z/2','deletion|right of upper cohomology diagram|simeq H2(BG,π)','deletion|below upper cohomology diagram|half W minus or equals 2g−2','diagram|middle black|integral and ζ coefficient squares; W prime to y','text|inside black square|Comm','text|right of black square lower line|unsure i','diagram|middle right blue|1 to ζ to G to G prime to 1','display|under blue exact row|H2(BG prime,ζ)','diagram|middle left underlined|X to BGd prime to BG prime','diagram|middle blue|H2(BG prime) containing E prime to H2(BT prime)','diagram|lower blue|X to Bπ to BG prime; GP and Sl containing circles','deletion|subscript of BT in lower blue diagram|unsure T double prime','insertion|below overwritten subscript|T prime','margin note|lower left|2g−2 ou g−1','margin note|lower right|E double prime maps to 2g−2; sim g−1','diagram|lower middle|Z simeq H2(X,Z), H2(π,Z), H2(BG prime,Z)','diagram|bottom blue|classifying spaces and H2 of the two tori','text|bottom left|329'],'''A diagram sheet on printed music paper, with black calculations above and blue comparisons below. The printed ruling is background, not additional manuscript mathematics. Top number 4; bottom manuscript/folio number 329. Both ink colours are treated as the same hand. The loose curved divider, two diagonal arrows and wavy stroke are reproduced, without assigning them mathematical labels.

The top-left groups compare G and G′, with a three-shaped central kernel ζ identified with Z/2Z and with discrete versions carrying d. The page explicitly writes Sl(2,R) and GP(2,R); the second digit is 2 even if a different naming convention would suggest GP(1,R). No tildes are visible above the two top G letters. The small unresolved mark belongs above their arrow. H’s fraktur-z is its typographic rendering of the same three-shaped kernel sign; ζ is used consistently here, distinguished from the narrow ξ class. This rendering convention is not counted as a separate disagreement at every occurrence.

The upper-right integral/coefficient diagrams compare W and half W, with an upward integer map labelled 2 and reductions toward ζ-valued cohomology. The two relevant degrees are 2, not H’s 4. Several connectors in C had been attached to the wrong grid cell: the diagonal from the BG′ integral node reaches the live BG′ coefficient node, and the long curve starts beneath the integral node and ends at the unfinished H2(X,...) on the right. The final coefficient and the small overwritten left coefficient remain uncertain. No missing right parenthesis is supplied. The crossed arithmetic fragment has cancellation on Z/2 itself; ·2=0 remains legible to its right.

In the second black square the arched line points toward W′ at the right, rather than back toward the integer at the left. “Comm” is live within the square: its apparent line-through is a staff rule. The bidirectional vertical arrow labelled 2 is retained as written. The blue middle target is H2(BT′), with neither a coefficient nor a comma after T′. The two horizontal relations from the Lie groups to circles are inclusion signs, not arrowheads. The lower-right marginal class has two primes, E′′, and the left margin says “2g−2 ou g−1”.

Targeted arithmetic check: 2g−2=2(g−1), so its reduction modulo 2 is zero; this explains why a factor-of-two comparison matters here, without deciding the uncertain cancelled equality sign. A multiplication-by-2 map between copies of Z sends a primitive generator to twice a generator. Thus labels such as half W or E′=half E require attention to which group the class lives in and to the chosen normalization; this leaf does not define all those choices, and no unqualified numerical value is imposed. The bottom comparison arrows reverse the displayed maps of classifying spaces as expected for H2. The cohomology identifications and the surface interpretation of 2g−2 are carried as the page’s background, not independently proved here.''',checks=[('136-328-even-integer','computation or formal certificate','2g−2=2(g−1); reduction modulo 2 is zero for integral g.'),('136-328-times-two','computation or formal certificate','The homomorphism n→2n on Z sends a generator to twice a generator; half-class notation depends on the ambient identification.'),('136-328-variance','targeted proof check','Bottom cohomology arrows run opposite the displayed maps X→Bπ→BG′ and BT′→BG′; checked domains and codomains only.'),('136-328-cohomology-identifications','carried as background without fault found','The stated H2 identifications and surface-class normalization are transcribed, not independently derived from this diagram-only leaf.')],habits=['Scan 328: printed staff rules can masquerade as cancellation, equality strokes or diagram edges. The live Comm inside the black square is an instance of C’s false cancellation. The kernel sign has a broad three-shaped outline and return loop; the class ξ is a narrow vertical zigzag. H explicitly chooses fraktur-z to render the kernel sign; this is treated as a rendering convention. Small 2s have rounded shoulders that can resemble n, and opening parentheses can make H2 appear H4. These readings were checked at the occurrences on this sheet, not assumed globally.'],notation=[('ζ versus ξ','Broad three-shaped kernel sign versus narrow descending zigzag class; retained distinction throughout this leaf.'),('staff rules','Printed grey parallel lines are excluded from ink arrows and deletions.'),('GP(2,R)','Digit 2 preserved despite the possible projective-dimension convention.'),('E prime / E double prime','Two primes in the right margin, single prime in the surrounding class diagrams.')],abbreviations=[('Comm','commutatif / commutative (diagram annotation)'),('Sl','special linear group notation as written'),('GP','projective group notation as written')],doubts=[('top G-to-G arrow label',r'\sim','short curved mark partly hidden by staff rule','low'),('upper-left coefficient',r'\mathbb Z/2',r'\zeta','low'),('crossed arithmetic first term',r'\mathbb Z/2','overwritten strokes','low'),('cancelled right expression relation',r'\simeq','crossed relation','low'),('unfinished H2(X,...) coefficient',r'\mathbb Z',r'\zeta','low'),('cancelled half-W sign','-','=','low'),('middle H2 first argument','X','retraced letter','low'),('isolated mark beside middle diagram','i','non-letter ink trace','low'),('overwritten blue BT subscript',"T''",'old subscript under heavy ink','low')],certainty=[('cancelled right coefficient',r'\unsure{\pi}',r'\pi','Two vertical legs share a flat top bar.',U,'high')])
